(begin-tx "DPTF-G3 — DPTF|C>X-BULK-TRANSFER: receivers and amounts must pair up")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G3 · 01 · bulk transfer arity] ---")
;;A bulk transfer takes a receiver list and an amount list positionally. If they differ in length
;;the pairing is meaningless — someone is paid the wrong amount or not at all — so the cap checks
;;the arity before reading anything about the token.
;;
;;Two DISTINCT receivers are used deliberately: UEV_IzUnique runs on the receiver list one line
;;ABOVE this guard, so a repeated receiver would trip the uniqueness check instead and this
;;assertion would be passing for the wrong reason.
;;==== DPTF-G3 — DPTF|C>X-BULK-TRANSFER: receivers and amounts must pair up · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G3 — DPTF|C>X-BULK-TRANSFER: receivers and amounts must pair up · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G3>> two receivers against one amount is refused"
            "Invalid Bulk Transfer Lists"
            (test-capability (TFT.DPTF|C>X-BULK-TRANSFER "a" "b" ["x" "y"] [1.0])))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

