(begin-tx "DPTF-G4 — module governance, the treasury-dispo domain, and the smart fee-target rule")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G4 · 01 · governance, dispo type, fee target] ---")
;;Three guards from three different bands, grouped because each needed its own route in.
;;
;;  GOV|DPTF_ADMIN          acquired DIRECTLY with test-capability — it is not an @event cap, so
;;                          no Talos call is needed. This is the gate governing DPTF upgrades.
;;  GOV|SET_TREASURY-DISPO  an @event cap, reached through the Talos ADMIN path with a bad type.
;;  DPTF|S>SET_FEE-TARGET   an @event cap, reached through the Talos CLIENT path.
;;
;;The fee-target case took three attempts and the message check caught each one. A STOA address was
;;rejected as a non-existent DALOS account; a standard Ouronet account goes down the OTHER branch
;;of the `if` entirely (it is checked for existence, not against the whitelist). The guard only
;;speaks for a SMART account, so the input is the VST smart-contract account — a real Σ. account
;;that is neither DALOS nor OUROBOROS.
;;==== DPTF-G4 — module governance, the treasury-dispo domain, and the smart fee-target rule · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G4 — module governance, the treasury-dispo domain, and the smart fee-target rule · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        ;;governance: EMMA is a real funded account, so this is "a legitimate user cannot upgrade
        ;;the module", not "an unknown key is refused".
        (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G4>> DPTF governance is refused for a legitimate but unprivileged signer"
            "DPTF Ownership not verified"
            (test-capability (DPTF.GOV|DPTF_ADMIN)))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

