(begin-tx "DPTF-G4b — treasury dispo type, and the smart-account fee-target whitelist")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G4b · 01 · dispo type and fee target] ---")
;;==== DPTF-G4b — treasury dispo type, and the smart-account fee-target whitelist · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G4b — treasury dispo type, and the smart-account fee-target whitelist · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
;;==== DPTF-G4b — treasury dispo type, and the smart-account fee-target whitelist · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G4b — treasury dispo type, and the smart-account fee-target whitelist · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
        (ref-TS01-C1:module{TalosStageOne_ClientOneV2} TS01-C1)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;--- the dispo type is a four-value enum; 9 is outside it
            (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G4b>> a treasury dispo type outside 0..3 is refused"
                "Treasury Dispo Type can only be 0, 1, 2 or 3!"
                (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_UpdateTreasuryDispoParameters KST.ANHD 9 1.0 1.0))
            ;;--- a SMART account may be a fee target only if it is DALOS or OUROBOROS. Fees accrue
            ;;to the target, and an arbitrary smart contract has no mechanism to disburse them —
            ;;so the whitelist is what stops fees being routed somewhere they can never leave.
            (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G4b>> an arbitrary SMART account cannot be made a fee target"
                "As Smart OURONET Accounts, only DALOS and OUROBOROS can be set as as fee Target"
                (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_SetFeeTarget KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto "MOCKA-98c486052a51") "MOCKA-98c486052a51"
                    (ref-DALOS::GOV|VST|SC_NAME)))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
;;BOTH OF THIS TX'S "NOT PINNED" ITEMS ARE NOW PINNED -- see DPTF-G6 below, which builds the
;;treasury-in-debt fixture they both needed. The analysis that said what the fixture had to be is
;;kept here because it is what made DPTF-G6 possible:
;;
;;  "A Type {} Treasury Dispo cannot be set at {} because it surpases the Current Treasury Value"
;;      CORRECTED 2026-09-11. An earlier note here said the 99999999.0 probe succeeded "because
;;      the treasury is larger than that", and that reaching the guard needs a value DERIVED from
;;      the live treasury. Both are wrong, and following that advice is a dead end: NO value of
;;      tdp/tds can trip this guard while the treasury is in credit.
;;
;;      Measured: the treasury's OURO supply here is 0.0, not something large. And
;;      UC_TreasuryLowestDispo returns (- 0.0 max-dispo) -- NEGATIVE by construction, for every
;;      type. The guard is (<= lowest-dispo treasury-supply), so a negative left side against a
;;      non-negative treasury is ALWAYS true; a tds of 1e9 gives lowest-dispo = -1e12, which
;;      passes comfortably.
;;
;;      What the guard actually means: a dispo ceiling may not be set so low that it fails to
;;      cover the treasury's EXISTING DEBT. It can only fire when treasury-supply is NEGATIVE --
;;      the same fixture the sibling guard below needs.
;;
;;  "Debt to be wiped must be smaller than or equal to the absolute value of the current Treasury
;;      Debt" sits behind "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury Balance", which is what answers while the
;;      treasury is in credit. It needs a treasury in DEBT.
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "DPTF-G6 — the treasury-in-debt fixture, and the four guards behind it")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G6 · 01 · credit state: the guards that answer first] ---")
;;The tx above closes with two guards recorded as unreachable: both need the treasury's OURO balance
;;to be NEGATIVE, and no call in the suite puts it there. I had written them off. That was wrong --
;;not about the fixture, about my options for building it.
;;
;;`env-module-admin` grants another module's admin INSIDE A REPL, so the balance can be written
;;directly; `rollback-tx` discards every write; and DPTF-G6b proves nothing leaked. The treasury's
;;OURO balance lives in DALOS, at DALOS|AccountTable[treasury]."ouroboros"."balance" -- so the admin
;;needed is DALOS's, not DPTF's.
;;
;;READ THIS BEFORE REUSING THE PATTERN: it grants in a REPL what no signer could grant on chain. It
;;is valid for pinning a guard's REACTION to a state, and says NOTHING about whether the state is
;;reachable in production. Keep those two claims apart -- conflating them is what produced two
;;withdrawn findings in this suite.
;;==== DPTF-G6 — the treasury-in-debt fixture, and the four guards behind it · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G6 — the treasury-in-debt fixture, and the four guards behind it · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs
    [ { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }
      ;;the treasury is a SMART account; UEV_SmartAccOwn's enforce-one accepts its SOVEREIGN's
      ;;guard, which is `ouronet-ns.dh_sc_dhvault-keyset` = PK_DHV. Without this signer the wipe
      ;;aborts in the mint with "Ownership could not be verified!" long before its own guards.
      { "key": "PK_DHV", "caps": [] }
    ]
)
;;==== DPTF-G6 — the treasury-in-debt fixture, and the four guards behind it · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G6 — the treasury-in-debt fixture, and the four guards behind it · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-DPTF:module{DemiourgosPactTrueFungibleV2} DPTF)
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
    )
    (let
        (
            (ouro:string (ref-DALOS::UR_OuroborosID))
            (treasury:string (at 0 (ref-DALOS::UR_DemiurgoiID)))
        )
        ;;--- the credit state first, because it is what makes the debt guards invisible. While the
        ;;    treasury is at 0.0 both wipe entrypoints answer with the SAME message, and the
        ;;    debt-size guard behind the partial one never gets a turn.
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> the treasury starts in credit, at exactly zero"
                    0.0 (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro treasury))
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G6>> wiping ALL debt is refused while the treasury is in credit"
                    "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury Balance" (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebt KST.ANHD))
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G6>> ...and so is wiping PART of it, with the same message"
                    "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury Balance"
                    (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebtPartial KST.ANHD 1.0))
            ]
        )
        (print "--- [DPTF-G6 · 02 · put the treasury 1,000,000 OURO into debt] ---")
        (env-module-admin DALOS)
        (update ref-DALOS::DALOS|AccountTable treasury
            { "ouroboros" :
                (+ { "balance" : -1000000.0 } (ref-DALOS::UR_TrueFungible treasury true)) })
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> the fixture took: the treasury is now in debt"
                    -1000000.0 (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro treasury))
                ;;--- GUARD 1, previously unreachable. "A dispo ceiling may not be set so low that
                ;;    it fails to cover existing debt." A type-3 dispo of tds=1.0 is a ceiling of
                ;;    1,000 OURO; the debt is 1,000,000. lowest-dispo is -1,000.0, which is NOT
                ;;    <= -1,000,000.0, so it fires.
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G6>> a dispo ceiling too small to cover the debt is refused"
                    "A Type 3 Treasury Dispo cannot be set at 1.0 because it surpases the Current Treasury Value of -1000000.0"
                    (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_UpdateTreasuryDispoParameters KST.ANHD 3 1.0 1.0))
                ;;...and the CONTRAST that makes it a threshold rather than "type 3 is broken". A
                ;;type-1 dispo is the whole OURO supply (1,986,000), which does cover the debt, so
                ;;the identical call shape is ACCEPTED in the identical state. Without this the
                ;;assertion above would also pass if the guard rejected everything.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> ...while a ceiling that DOES cover it is accepted in the same state"
                    "Write succeeded" (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_UpdateTreasuryDispoParameters KST.ANHD 1 0.0 0.0))
                ;;--- GUARD 2, previously unreachable. Now that the treasury is in debt the
                ;;    positive-balance guard passes and the debt-SIZE guard finally answers. 0.1
                ;;    over the debt is enough: this is a boundary, not a magnitude test.
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G6>> wiping more than the actual debt is refused"
                    "Debt to be wiped must be smaller than or equal to the absolute value of the current Treasury Debt"
                    (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebtPartial KST.ANHD 1000000.1))
            ]
        )
        (print "--- [DPTF-G6 · 03 · the wipe paths actually execute] ---")
        ;;Both wipe entrypoints had never run anywhere in the suite -- only their refusals had. A
        ;;guard proven to refuse is half a test; these two assertions are the other half.
        (map print
            [
                ;;a PARTIAL wipe mints exactly the requested amount back to the treasury, so the
                ;;debt shrinks by that much and no more. Asserted on the arithmetic, not on
                ;;"it returned something".
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> a partial wipe reduces the debt by exactly the amount wiped"
                    -600000.0
                    (let ((ignore (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebtPartial KST.ANHD 400000.0)))
                        (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro treasury)))
                ;;...and a full wipe clears whatever remains, to exactly zero. It mints
                ;;(abs treasury-supply), so the result is 0.0 for any starting debt.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> a full wipe clears the remaining debt to exactly zero"
                    0.0
                    (let ((ignore (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebt KST.ANHD)))
                        (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro treasury)))
                ;;A_WipeTreasuryDebt also resets the dispo parameters via XE_UpdateTreasury 0 0.0
                ;;0.0 -- which is the whole reason this transaction must not commit. DPTF-G6b is
                ;;the check that it did not.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G6>> ...and a full wipe also resets the dispo parameters to type 0"
                    [0 0.0 0.0]
                    [(ref-DALOS::UR_DispoType) (ref-DALOS::UR_DispoTDP) (ref-DALOS::UR_DispoTDS)])
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
;;ROLLBACK, never commit: this transaction fabricated a debt, changed the dispo type twice and
;;minted 1,000,000 OURO.
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "DPTF-G6b — the debt fixture left no trace")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G6b · 01 · no leakage] ---")
;;DPTF-G6 wrote a sovereign balance directly, minted against it and reset the dispo parameters. A
;;`commit-tx` typo there would hand every later suite a treasury with 1,000,000 OURO of phantom
;;supply and a type-0 dispo, and nothing downstream would question it. Cheap to assert, so asserted.
(map print
    [
        (expect "<<DPTF-G6b>> the treasury is back in credit at zero"
            0.0 (DPTF.UR_AccountSupply (DALOS.UR_OuroborosID) (at 0 (DALOS.UR_DemiurgoiID))))
        (expect "<<DPTF-G6b>> ...and the dispo parameters are the originals, not the wiped ones"
            [3 320.0 250.0]
            [(DALOS.UR_DispoType) (DALOS.UR_DispoTDP) (DALOS.UR_DispoTDS)])
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
