(begin-tx "DPTF-G7 — the OURO dispo floor, and why its sibling guard cannot fire")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPTF-G7 · 01 · the dispo floor on an OURO wipe] ---")
;;DPTF|C>DEBIT carries two OURO-only guards, both previously recorded here as needing "OURO
;;treasury/dispo state this suite does not reach". One of them does not need any such state; the
;;other cannot fire at all. Both conclusions come from execution, below.
;;
;;WHAT MAKES THE DEBIT PATH OURO-SPECIFIC. For OURO alone, DPTF|C>DEBIT computes a `lowest-dispo`
;;floor and allows the balance to go BELOW ZERO down to it -- OURO is the one token whose balances
;;may be negative (the dispo is a credit line). The floor depends on the account:
;;    * the TREASURY            -> URC_TreasuryLowestDispo (negative; a real credit line)
;;    * any other smart account -> 0.0
;;    * a standard account      -> (- (UC_OuroDispo dispo-data))
;;
;;GUARD 1 -- "Cannot Debit OURO from {}, dispo capabilities exceeded!" -- IS reachable, and cheaply:
;;freeze a standard account's OURO and wipe more than it holds. Every wipe path passes
;;UDC_EmptyDispo, whose UC_OuroDispo is 0.0, so the floor is 0.0 and any over-wipe breaches it.
;;The freeze is required first by DPTF|C>X_WIPE (UEV_AccountFreezeState … true).
;;==== DPTF-G7 — the OURO dispo floor, and why its sibling guard cannot fire · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G7 — the OURO dispo floor, and why its sibling guard cannot fire · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
;;==== DPTF-G7 — the OURO dispo floor, and why its sibling guard cannot fire · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPTF-G7 — the OURO dispo floor, and why its sibling guard cannot fire · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-DPTF:module{DemiourgosPactTrueFungibleV2} DPTF)
        (ref-TS01-C1:module{TalosStageOne_ClientOneV2} TS01-C1)
        (ref-U|DPTF:module{UtilityDptfV2} U|DPTF)
    )
    (let
        (
            (ouro:string (ref-DALOS::UR_OuroborosID))
            (treasury:string (at 0 (ref-DALOS::UR_DemiurgoiID)))
        )
        (map print
            [
                ;;the floor every wipe actually uses. Asserted because the whole argument below
                ;;turns on it being ZERO and not negative.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> a wipe's dispo-data is empty, so its OURO floor is 0.0"
                    0.0 (ref-U|DPTF::UC_OuroDispo (ref-U|DPTF::UDC_EmptyDispo)))
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> the target is a STANDARD account, which is the 0.0-floor branch"
                    false (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountType KST.ANHD))
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> ...and it holds OURO to wipe"
                    true (> (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro KST.ANHD) 0.0))
            ]
        )
        ;;the wipe refuses outright on an unfrozen account, so freeze first. That refusal is pinned
        ;;elsewhere; here it is just a precondition.
        (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_ToggleFreezeAccount KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) KST.ANHD ouro true)
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> the account is now frozen, which is what the wipe requires"
                    true (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountFrozenState ouro KST.ANHD))
                ;;GUARD 1, previously unpinned. 9,000,000 against a balance of ~1,567,573 drives
                ;;debit-result to roughly -7.4M, far under the 0.0 floor.
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G7>> wiping more OURO than the dispo floor allows is refused"
                    "dispo capabilities exceeded!"
                    (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_WipeSlim KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) KST.ANHD ouro 9000000.0))
                ;;...and the contrast, so the assertion is a threshold and not "wipes never work".
                ;;Wiping exactly 1.0 keeps debit-result positive, so the floor is not reached.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> ...while a wipe that stays above the floor succeeds"
                    true
                    (let ((before:decimal (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro KST.ANHD)))
                        (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_WipeSlim KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) KST.ANHD ouro 1.0)
                        (= (- before 1.0) (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro KST.ANHD))))
            ]
        )
        (print "--- [DPTF-G7 · 02 · guard 2 is UNREACHABLE, and here is the proof] ---")
        ;;GUARD 2 -- "Can only Debit positive OURO Amounts", at 05_DPTF.pact:951 --
        ;;    (if (and (= id ouro-id) wipe-mode) (enforce (> current-supply 0.0) …) true)
        ;;cannot be tripped by any input. Four facts, each asserted below or verified by grep, close
        ;;every way in. This is NOT "we lack a fixture" -- it is dead by construction.
        ;;
        ;;  (a) It needs wipe-mode TRUE. wipe-mode is a parameter of XB_DebitTrueFungible, and every
        ;;      caller is known: the two in-module wipe paths (DPTF|C>X_WIPE, via C_Wipe and
        ;;      C_WipeSlim) pass TRUE, and all five external call sites -- all in 09_TFT.pact, lines
        ;;      1355/1368/1380/1779/1846 -- pass FALSE. So wipe-mode TRUE implies the wipe path.
        ;;  (b) The wipe path always passes UDC_EmptyDispo, so the floor is 0.0 for every account
        ;;      EXCEPT the treasury (asserted above).
        ;;  (c) The treasury is excluded anyway: a wipe requires the account FROZEN, freezing runs
        ;;      DALOS::UEV_NotSmartOuronetAccount, and the treasury is a SMART account. It can never
        ;;      be frozen, so it can never be wiped. Asserted below.
        ;;  (d) UEV_Amount -- the first thing DPTF|C>DEBIT calls -- forces amount > 0.0.
        ;;
        ;;Compose them: guard 1 (floor 0.0) demands current-supply - amount >= 0, and (d) gives
        ;;amount > 0, so reaching guard 2 at all requires current-supply > 0 -- which is exactly the
        ;;condition guard 2 tests. Whenever it is consulted it passes. A fail-closed backstop.
        ;;
        ;;NOTE for whoever revisits it: the guard's CONDITION tests current-supply while its MESSAGE
        ;;names the amount -- a message/code mismatch of the kind already annotated on
        ;;OUROBOROS::URCv_Sublimate. If the intent was `(> amount 0.0)`, (d) already enforces that,
        ;;so the guard would still be redundant. PROPOSED, not applied: annotate 951 `;;UNREACHABLE`.
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPTF-G7>> (c) the treasury is a SMART account"
                    true (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountType treasury))
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G7>> (c) ...so it can never be frozen, hence never wiped"
                    "Non Smart Ouronet Accounts required for exec"
                    (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_ToggleFreezeAccount KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) treasury ouro true))
                ;;(d) the amount gate that closes the last door, asserted on both a zero and a
                ;;negative amount since the guard would need one of them.
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G7>> (d) a zero-amount wipe is refused before any dispo math"
                    "is not a Valid Transaction amount"
                    (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_WipeSlim KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) KST.ANHD ouro 0.0))
                (expect-failure "<<DPTF-G7>> (d) ...and so is a negative one"
                    "is not a Valid Transaction amount"
                    (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_WipeSlim KST.ANHD (DPTF.UR_Konto ouro) KST.ANHD ouro -5.0))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
;;this tx froze an account and wiped 1.0 OURO out of existence; DPTF-G9 checks it all came back.
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
