(begin-tx "DPTF-G14a — CONTROL: the overdraft alone is permitted")
(print "")
(print "=== DPTF-G14 — dispo-data is recomputed for EVERY leg =======================")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;M5 / #29M (ranked MEDIUM, and the chapter calls it under-ranked): `dispo-data` was snapshotted ONCE
;;before the multi-transfer fold and reused for every leg. An account's permitted OURO OVERDRAFT is a
;;function of its Elite-Auryn holdings, so a leg that sends Elite-Auryn away leaves every LATER leg
;;in the same batch checking against a stale, too-generous limit -- real OURO-overdraft inflation.
;;The fix recomputes it inside each leg's own `let` (`09_TFT.pact:1797`, `:1867`).
;;
;;It was present and unwitnessed. <<DPTF-G7>> pins the OURO dispo FLOOR on a wipe -- a different
;;guard on a different path. No test had ever built a batch combining an EA-REDUCING leg with an
;;overdraft leg, which is the only shape that distinguishes the fixed code from the broken code.
;;
;;THE TWO HALVES ARE IN SEPARATE TRANSACTIONS, and that is not cosmetic. `expect-failure` does NOT
;;roll back REPL writes: with both halves in one transaction the refused batch's FIRST leg (the
;;Elite-Auryn drain) still lands, and the control then fails for the very reason it is meant to
;;disprove. That is what the first draft of this block did -- a control that fails looks like a
;;broken test, not like a contaminated one.
;;
;;[a] CONTROL FIRST: 1,580,000 OURO alone -- more than the sender holds -- SUCCEEDS, landing around
;;-12,426. A legitimate overdraft, backed by ~114,907 Elite-Auryn.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DPTF:module{DemiourgosPactTrueFungibleV2} DPTF)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-TS01-C1:module{TalosStageOne_ClientOneV2} TS01-C1)
        (ouro:string "OURO-98c486052a51")
        (overdraft:decimal 1580000.0)
    )
    (let
        (
            (elite-auryn:string (ref-DALOS::UR_EliteAurynID))
            (ouro-held:decimal (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro KST.ANHD))
        )
        (map print
            [
                ;;PRECONDITIONS: it must really be an overdraft, and the backing must really exist.
                (expect "<<DPTF-G14>> the amount really exceeds the sender's OURO, so it IS an overdraft"
                    true (> overdraft ouro-held))
                (expect "<<DPTF-G14>> ...and the sender really holds the Elite-Auryn that permits it"
                    true (> (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply elite-auryn KST.ANHD) 0.0))
            ]
        )
        (ref-TS01-C1::DPTF|C_MultiTransfer KST.ANHD KST.ANHD KST.EMMA [ouro] [overdraft] false)
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPTF-G14>> CONTROL: the overdraft ALONE is permitted, backed by the Elite-Auryn"
                    true (< (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply ouro KST.ANHD) 0.0))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

